the target language is: prolog.

% Small fixture for the debugger/trace tests: a query with SEVERAL answers (so all
% answers must be traceable) and a rule using "for all cases in which" (so the
% forall must stay on the call stack while its condition/consequent run).

the templates are:
    *a person* is happy.
    *a person* is rich.
    *a person* has *a friend*.
    *a person* is friendly.

the knowledge base trace includes:
    A person is happy
        if the person is rich.

    A person is friendly
        if for all cases in which
            the person has a friend
        it is the case that
            the friend is rich.

scenario s is:
    alice is rich.
    bob is rich.
    alice has bob.
    happy expects answers ["alice is happy", "bob is happy"].
    friendly expects answers ["alice is friendly"].

query happy is:
    which person is happy.

query friendly is:
    which person is friendly.
